    "knowledge_point": "Calculating the Slope of the Tangent to a Circle",
    "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062909/assets/f24d078ca0dc57ebd12778b7862683b0289e9c0d4c664639bd210dcc1f7c6d1b.png)\n\nFind $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for the circle shown above.",
    "worked_solution": "Since our circle is centered at the origin and has a radius of $4,$ its equation is given by\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}={4}^{2}\\,⟹\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=16.\n$$\n\nNow, to calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(16) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({y}^{2}) & =0 \\\\ 2x+2y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =0 \\\\ 2y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-2x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{x}{y}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
